Z||000003||BN Boomer||11-12-2001||02:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>i've always heard warnings of shady used car dealers adding sawdust. don't know if you can clean it out later during a rebuild or if it ruins it permenently. not planning to try it or find out i am trying it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That only works in differentials, manual transmissions, and transfer cases. Basically anything that only contains gears, not valve bodies and/or clutches. Not automatic transaxles or transmissions, in which the sawdust would immediately clog up the various passages and the fluid would be unable to flow.<BR>||||reg||1
